-- Retired: the SQL word-case surface chain
--   word_case_class_surface(word) -> word_case_map_surface(word, map)
--     -> grapheme_case_target(grapheme, map)
-- is superseded by the shared native batch owner in src/lexical_case.c:
-- lexical.word_case_variants serves variant lookup, while
-- lexical.word_case_classes_batch serves the shape-peer lower-surface gate.
-- The old chain fanned one lexical lookup into O(3 * graphemes) non-inlinable
-- consensus LIMIT-1 subqueries plus O(graphemes) realize.render_text SPI calls (the RBAR on
-- the hot senses/define/bubble_up path). Shape recall now also uses the native
-- set owner; these retired scalar bodies must not be restored as a fallback.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace.word_case_class_surface(bytea);
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace.word_case_map_surface(bytea, text);
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace.grapheme_case_target(bytea, text);
